<resources>
    <!--
    Without a declared theme, Android fell back to the system default (with an ActionBar) — the
    platform itself drew a native bar with the app label ("Rateio") on top of the real UI,
    duplicating the `TopAppBar` each Compose screen already draws (found while porting the
    prototype's theme toggle: every TopAppBar got a sun/moon button, and the ghost native bar
    would have been left floating on top). NoActionBar removes that native bar; every real
    color/decoration still comes from Compose (RateioTheme), never from this theme — it only
    exists to turn off the system chrome.
    -->
    <style name="Theme.Rateio" parent="android:Theme.Material.Light.NoActionBar" />
</resources>
